    {
      "image": "videos/05-brain-washes-itself/2.jpg",
      "seconds": 20.55,
      "text": "Every organ in your body has lymphatic plumbing to flush out waste. For a century, the brain appeared to have none. Then in twenty thirteen, researchers at Rochester found the system had been hiding in plain sight. During sleep, the spaces between brain cells open up, and cerebrospinal fluid floods through, carrying metabolic debris out. They named it the glymphatic system.",
      "delivery": {
        "rate": 12,
        "pitch": 0
      },
      "clips": [
        {
          "src": "videos/05-brain-washes-itself/v2-1.mp3",
          "atMs": 0
        },
        {
